{"id":"mahabharata-12-221","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":221,"title":"एकविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 221 · Signs of rise and fall","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for the signs of a man's coming fortune and ruin. Bhishma tells how Sri told Indra which men she dwells with and which she leaves, such as quarrelsome households and those who rise late.","kn":"ಮನುಷ್ಯನ ಬರುವ ಅದೃಷ್ಟ, ನಾಶದ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶ್ರೀ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಯಾರೊಡನೆ ವಾಸಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಯಾರನ್ನು ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಜಗಳಗಂಟರ ಮನೆ, ತಡವಾಗಿ ಏಳುವವರೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर मनुष्य के आने वाले भाग्य और विनाश के लक्षण पूछते हैं। भीष्म बताते हैं कि श्री ने इन्द्र से कहा कि वह किनके साथ रहती है और किन्हें छोड़ती है, जैसे झगड़ालू घर और देर से उठने वाले।","te":"మనిషికి రాబోయే అదృష్టం, నాశనం లక్షణాలను యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. శ్రీ ఇంద్రునికి ఎవరితో ఉంటుందో, ఎవరిని విడుస్తుందో, కలహాల ఇళ్లు, ఆలస్యంగా లేచేవారని భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மனிதனுக்கு வரவிருக்கும் செழிப்பும் அழிவும் குறித்த அடையாளங்களை யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, ஸ்ரீ இந்திரனிடம் யாருடன் வசிக்கிறாள், யாரை விடுகிறாள் என்று கூறியதைப் பீஷ்மர் விவரிக்கிறார், சண்டையிடும் வீடுகள், தாமதமாக எழுவோர் போன்றோர்.","ml":"മനുഷ്യന്റെ ഭാഗ്യത്തിന്റെയും നാശത്തിന്റെയും ലക്ഷണങ്ങൾ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കലഹമുള്ള കുടുംബങ്ങളെയും വൈകി ഉണരുന്നവരെയും പോലെ, ശ്രീ ഏതു മനുഷ്യരോടൊപ്പം വസിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും ആരെ വിട്ടുപോകുന്നുവെന്നും ഇന്ദ്രനോട് പറഞ്ഞതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.221; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पूर्वरूपाणि मे राजन्पुरुषस्य भविष्यतः ।\nपराभविष्यतश्चैव त्वं मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, grandfather, tell me the signs that come before a man's rise and before his fall."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"मन एव मनुष्यस्य पूर्वरूपाणि शंसति ।\nभविष्यतश्च भद्रं ते तथैव नभविष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mind of a man itself announces the signs of what will and will not be; may good come to you."}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nश्रिया शक्रस्य संवादं तन्निबोध युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they tell this ancient account, the conversation of Indra and Shri; hear it, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":4,"text":"महतस्तपसो व्युष्ट्या पश्यँल्लोकौ परावरौ ।\nसामान्यमृषिभिर्गत्वा ब्रह्मलोकनिवासिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the fruit of great austerity, Narada, seeing both the higher and lower worlds, went like Brahma himself, of boundless radiance, sinless and of great austerity, having gone with the sages who dwell in Brahma's world,"}},{"n":5,"text":"ब्रह्मैवामितदीप्तौजाः शान्तपाप्मा महातपाः ।\nविचचार यथाकामं त्रिषु लोकेषु नारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and roamed as he wished through the three worlds."}},{"n":6,"text":"कदाचित्प्रातरुत्थाय पिस्पृक्षुः सलिलं शुचि ।\nध्रुवद्वारभवां गङ्गां जगामावततार च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, rising in the morning, wishing to touch pure water, he went down to the Ganga that springs from Dhruva's gate."}},{"n":7,"text":"सहस्रनयनश्चापि वज्री शम्बरपाकहा ।\nतस्या देवर्षिजुष्टायास्तीरमभ्याजगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thousand-eyed wielder of the thunderbolt, slayer of Shambara and Paka, also came to the bank of that river, frequented by divine sages."}},{"n":8,"text":"तावाप्लुत्य यतात्मानौ कृतजप्यौ समासतुः ।\nनद्याः पुलिनमासाद्य सूक्ष्मकाञ्चनवालुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed, the two self-controlled ones, after reciting their prayers, sat on the river's bank, whose sand was fine as gold."}},{"n":9,"text":"पुण्यकर्मभिराख्याता देवर्षिकथिताः कथाः ।\nचक्रतुस्तौ कथाशीलौ शुचिसंहृष्टमानसौ ।\nपूर्ववृत्तव्यपेतानि कथयन्तौ समाहितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fond of stories, pure and glad in mind, they told tales related by those of holy deeds and spoken by divine sages, recounting things from former times, concentrated."}},{"n":10,"text":"अथ भास्करमुद्यन्तं रश्मिजालपुरस्कृतम् ।\nपूर्णमण्डलमालोक्य तावुत्थायोपतस्थतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they saw the sun rising, with its net of rays before it, its full disc, and rose and stood to honour it."}},{"n":11,"text":"अभितस्तूदयन्तं तमर्कमर्कमिवापरम् ।\nआकाशे ददृशे ज्योतिरुद्यतार्चिःसमप्रभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On all sides, in the sky, a light was seen, like another sun rising, with blazing flames."}},{"n":12,"text":"तयोः समीपं संप्राप्तं प्रत्यदृश्यत भारत ।\nतत्सुपर्णार्कचरितमास्थितं वैष्णवं पदम् ।\nभाभिरप्रतिमं भाति त्रैलोक्यमवभासयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It came near them, Bharata: a light, the path of Vishnu, travelled by Garuda and the sun, shining without equal and lighting the three worlds."}},{"n":13,"text":"दिव्याभिरूपशोभाभिरप्सरोभिः पुरस्कृताम् ।\nबृहतीमंशुमत्प्रख्यां बृहद्भानोरिवार्चिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was led by apsarases of divine form and beauty, a vast radiance like the flames of the great sun."}},{"n":14,"text":"नक्षत्रकल्पाभरणां ताराभक्तिसमस्रजम् ।\nश्रियं ददृशतुः पद्मां साक्षात्पद्मतलस्थिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw Shri, the lotus goddess, adorned like the constellations, wearing a garland like rows of stars, standing as if on a lotus."}},{"n":15,"text":"सावरुह्य विमानाग्रादङ्गनानामनुत्तमा ।\nअभ्यगच्छत्त्रिलोकेशं शक्रं चर्षिं च नारदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of women, she descended from the front of the heavenly car and approached Indra, lord of the three worlds, and the sage Narada."}},{"n":16,"text":"नारदानुगतः साक्षान्मघवांस्तामुपागमत् ।\nकृताञ्जलिपुटो देवीं निवेद्यात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Followed by Narada, Maghavan himself approached the goddess, with joined palms, presenting himself."}},{"n":17,"text":"चक्रे चानुपमां पूजां तस्याश्चापि स सर्ववित् ।\nदेवराजः श्रियं राजन्वाक्यं चेदमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the all-knowing king of the gods paid her matchless honour, and said these words to Shri, O king."}},{"n":18,"text":"का त्वं केन च कार्येण संप्राप्ता चारुहासिनि ।\nकुतश्चागम्यते सुभ्रु गन्तव्यं क्व च ते शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Who are you, and for what purpose have you come, lovely-smiling one? From where do you come, fair-browed, and where, auspicious one, are you going?'"}},{"text":"श्रीरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shri said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"पुण्येषु त्रिषु लोकेषु सर्वे स्थावरजङ्गमाः ।\nममात्मभावमिच्छन्तो यतन्ते परमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the holy three worlds, all things moving and unmoving strive, with the supreme self, to attain my state."}},{"n":20,"text":"साहं वै पङ्कजे जाता सूर्यरश्मिविबोधिते ।\nभूत्यर्थं सर्वभूतानां पद्मा श्रीः पद्ममालिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am born in the lotus awakened by the sun's rays, Padma, Shri, wearing a lotus garland, for the prosperity of all beings."}},{"n":21,"text":"अहं लक्ष्मीरहं भूतिः श्रीश्चाहं बलसूदन ।\nअहं श्रद्धा च मेधा च सन्नतिर्विजितिः स्थितिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Lakshmi, I am Bhuti, I am Shri, slayer of Bala; I am faith and intelligence, humility, victory and steadiness."}},{"n":22,"text":"अहं धृतिरहं सिद्धिरहं त्विड्भूतिरेव च ।\nअहं स्वाहा स्वधा चैव संस्तुतिर्नियतिः कृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am constancy, I am success, I am splendour and prosperity; I am Svaha and Svadha, praise, destiny and action."}},{"n":23,"text":"राज्ञां विजयमानानां सेनाग्रेषु ध्वजेषु च ।\nनिवासे धर्मशीलानां विषयेषु पुरेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I dwell at the head of the armies of victorious kings and on their banners, in the homes of the righteous, and in lands and cities."}},{"n":24,"text":"जितकाशिनि शूरे च संग्रामेष्वनिवर्तिनि ।\nनिवसामि मनुष्येन्द्रे सदैव बलसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I always dwell, slayer of Bala, in a king who is victorious, heroic, and never turns back in battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"धर्मनित्ये महाबुद्धौ ब्रह्मण्ये सत्यवादिनि ।\nप्रश्रिते दानशीले च सदैव निवसाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I dwell always in the man who is constant in dharma, of great understanding, devoted to Brahmanas, truthful, humble and generous."}},{"n":26,"text":"असुरेष्ववसं पूर्वं सत्यधर्मनिबन्धना ।\nविपरीतांस्तु तान्बुद्ध्वा त्वयि वासमरोचयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Formerly I dwelt among the asuras, bound by truth and dharma; but finding them reversed, I chose to dwell with you."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"कथंवृत्तेषु दैत्येषु त्वमवात्सीर्वरानने ।\nदृष्ट्वा च किमिहागास्त्वं हित्वा दैतेयदानवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fair-faced one, how did the Daityas behave that you lived among them, and seeing what have you left the Daityas and Danavas and come here?"}},{"text":"श्रीरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shri said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"स्वधर्ममनुतिष्ठत्सु धैर्यादचलितेषु च ।\nस्वर्गमार्गाभिरामेषु सत्त्वेषु निरता ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I delighted in beings who followed their own dharma, unshaken by steadiness, and pleased by the path to heaven."}},{"n":29,"text":"दानाध्ययनयज्ञेज्या गुरुदैवतपूजनम् ।\nविप्राणामतिथीनां च तेषां नित्यमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving, study, sacrifice, honouring teachers and gods, and service of Brahmanas and guests went on constantly among them."}},{"n":30,"text":"सुसंमृष्टगृहाश्चासञ्जितस्त्रीका हुताग्नयः ।\nगुरुशुश्रूषवो दान्ता ब्रह्मण्याः सत्यवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their houses were well swept, they had mastered their wives, kept the sacred fires, served teachers, were self-controlled, devoted to Brahmanas, and truthful."}},{"n":31,"text":"श्रद्दधाना जितक्रोधा दानशीलानसूयकाः ।\nभृतपुत्रा भृतामात्या भृतदारा ह्यनीर्षवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Faithful, with anger conquered, generous and free of envy, they supported sons, ministers and wives, without jealousy."}},{"n":32,"text":"अमर्षणा न चान्योन्यं स्पृहयन्ति कदाचन ।\nन च जातूपतप्यन्ते धीराः परसमृद्धिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Patient, they never coveted one another's things, and the steadfast were never pained at others' prosperity."}},{"n":33,"text":"दातारः संगृहीतार आर्याः करुणवेदिनः ।\nमहाप्रसादा ऋजवो दृढभक्ता जितेन्द्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were givers and gatherers, noble, understanding of compassion, very gracious, upright, firmly devoted, masters of their senses."}},{"n":34,"text":"संतुष्टभृत्यसचिवाः कृतज्ञाः प्रियवादिनः ।\nयथार्थमानार्थकरा ह्रीनिषेधा यतव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their servants and ministers were content; they were grateful and sweet-spoken, giving honour and wealth as due, modest, firm in vows."}},{"n":35,"text":"नित्यं पर्वसु सुस्नाताः स्वनुलिप्ताः स्वलंकृताः ।\nउपवासतपःशीलाः प्रतीता ब्रह्मवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On festival days they bathed well, anointed and adorned themselves well, kept fasts and austerities, and were known as speakers on Brahman."}},{"n":36,"text":"नैनानभ्युदियात्सूर्यो न चाप्यासन्प्रगेनिशाः ।\nरात्रौ दधि च सक्तूंश्च नित्यमेव व्यवर्जयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun never rose upon them sleeping, nor did they sleep at dawn; at night they always avoided curd and barley meal."}},{"n":37,"text":"काल्यं घृतं चान्ववेक्षन्प्रयता ब्रह्मचारिणः ।\nमङ्गलानपि चापश्यन्ब्राह्मणांश्चाप्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pure and celibate, they looked at the morning ghee, saw auspicious things and honoured Brahmanas."}},{"n":38,"text":"सदा हि ददतां धर्मः सदा चाप्रतिगृह्णताम् ।\nअर्धं च रात्र्याः स्वपतां दिवा चास्वपतां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who always give and never receive, who sleep half the night and not by day, there is always dharma."}},{"n":39,"text":"कृपणानाथवृद्धानां दुर्बलातुरयोषिताम् ।\nदायं च संविभागं च नित्यमेवानुमोदताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They always approved giving and sharing with the wretched, helpless, elderly, weak, sick and women."}},{"n":40,"text":"विषण्णं त्रस्तमुद्विग्नं भयार्तं व्याधिपीडितम् ।\nहृतस्वं व्यसनार्तं च नित्यमाश्वासयन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They always comforted those who were dejected, frightened, anxious, afraid, afflicted by illness, robbed of their property or hit by calamity."}},{"n":41,"text":"धर्ममेवान्ववर्तन्त न हिंसन्ति परस्परम् ।\nअनुकूलाश्च कार्येषु गुरुवृद्धोपसेविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They followed dharma alone and did not harm one another; they were agreeable in tasks and served teachers and elders."}},{"n":42,"text":"पितृदेवातिथींश्चैव यथावत्तेऽभ्यपूजयन् ।\nअवशेषाणि चाश्नन्ति नित्यं सत्यतपोरताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They properly honoured ancestors, gods and guests, and always ate what remained, devoted to truth and austerity."}},{"n":43,"text":"नैकेऽश्नन्ति सुसंपन्नं न गच्छन्ति परस्त्रियम् ।\nसर्वभूतेष्ववर्तन्त यथात्मनि दयां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not eat well-prepared food alone, did not go to another's wife, and behaved toward all beings with the compassion they had for themselves."}},{"n":44,"text":"नैवाकाशे न पशुषु नायोनौ न च पर्वसु ।\nइन्द्रियस्य विसर्गं तेऽरोचयन्त कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"They never favoured the discharge of seed in the open air, among animals, in the wrong womb, or on sacred days."}},{"n":45,"text":"नित्यं दानं तथा दाक्ष्यमार्जवं चैव नित्यदा ।\nउत्साहश्चानहंकारः परमं सौहृदं क्षमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving always, skill, uprightness always, energy without ego, supreme friendliness and patience:"}},{"n":46,"text":"सत्यं दानं तपः शौचं कारुण्यं वागनिष्ठुरा ।\nमित्रेषु चानभिद्रोहः सर्वं तेष्वभवत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"truth, giving, austerity, purity, compassion, gentle speech, and no treachery toward friends: all this was in them, lord."}},{"n":47,"text":"निद्रा तन्द्रीरसंप्रीतिरसूया चानवेक्षिता ।\nअरतिश्च विषादश्च न स्पृहा चाविशन्त तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sleep, drowsiness, dislike, envy, carelessness, discontent, despair and craving did not enter them."}},{"n":48,"text":"साहमेवंगुणेष्वेव दानवेष्ववसं पुरा ।\nप्रजासर्गमुपादाय नैकं युगविपर्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I lived formerly among Danavas who had such qualities, from the beginning of creation through more than one turning of the ages."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततः कालविपर्यासे तेषां गुणविपर्ययात् ।\nअपश्यं विगतं धर्मं कामक्रोधवशात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the turning of time, as their qualities reversed, I saw dharma depart from those ruled by desire and anger."}},{"n":50,"text":"सभासदां ते वृद्धानां सत्याः कथयतां कथाः ।\nप्राहसन्नभ्यसूयंश्च सर्ववृद्धान्गुणावराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When elders in the assembly told true stories, the lesser in qualities laughed at them and scorned all the elders."}},{"n":51,"text":"यूनः सहसमासीनान्वृद्धानभिगतान्सतः ।\nनाभ्युत्थानाभिवादाभ्यां यथापूर्वमपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not rise or greet the elderly good men who came where the young were sitting, as they used to."}},{"n":52,"text":"वर्तयन्त्येव पितरि पुत्राः प्रभवताऽऽत्मनः ।\nअमित्रभृत्यतां प्राप्य ख्यापयन्तोऽनपत्रपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sons began to treat their fathers as though they were masters; they became enemies and servants and proclaimed it shamelessly."}},{"n":53,"text":"तथा धर्मादपेतेन कर्मणा गर्हितेन ये ।\nमहतः प्राप्नुवन्त्यर्थांस्तेष्वेषामभवत्स्पृहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They also coveted what those who, through blameworthy and unrighteous action, gain great wealth, had."}},{"n":54,"text":"उच्चैश्चाप्यवदन्रात्रौ नीचैस्तत्राग्निरज्वलत् ।\nपुत्राः पितॄनभ्यवदन्भार्याश्चाभ्यवदन्पतीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They spoke loudly at night, the fire burned low, sons spoke harshly to fathers and wives to husbands."}},{"n":55,"text":"मातरं पितरं वृद्धमाचार्यमतिथिं गुरुम् ।\nगुरुवन्नाभ्यनन्दन्त कुमारान्नान्वपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not welcome mother, father, the old, the teacher, the guest or elders as they should, and did not look after their children."}},{"n":56,"text":"भिक्षां बलिमदत्त्वा च स्वयमन्नानि भुञ्जते ।\nअनिष्ट्वा संविभज्याथ पितृदेवातिथीन्गुरून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without giving alms or offerings, they ate food themselves, without sacrificing or sharing with ancestors, gods, guests and teachers."}},{"n":57,"text":"न शौचमनुरुध्यन्त तेषां सूदजनास्तथा ।\nमनसा कर्मणा वाचा भक्तमासीदनावृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not care for cleanliness; their cooks in thought, deed and word left the food uncovered."}},{"n":58,"text":"विप्रकीर्णानि धान्यानि काकमूषकभोजनम् ।\nअपावृतं पयोऽतिष्ठदुच्छिष्टाश्चास्पृशन्घृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scattered grain became food for crows and mice; milk stood uncovered, and they touched ghee while impure."}},{"n":59,"text":"कुद्दालपाटीपिटकं प्रकीर्णं कांस्यभाजनम् ।\nद्रव्योपकरणं सर्वं नान्ववैक्षत्कुटुम्बिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hoes, baskets, and bronze vessels lay scattered; the housewife did not look after any of the household's goods and tools."}},{"n":60,"text":"प्राकारागारविध्वंसान्न स्म ते प्रतिकुर्वते ।\nनाद्रियन्ते पशून्बद्ध्वा यवसेनोदकेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not repair damaged walls and houses, nor did they care to tie up the cattle and give them fodder and water."}},{"n":61,"text":"बालानां प्रेक्षमाणानां स्वयं भक्षानभक्षयन् ।\nतथा भृत्यजनं सर्वं पर्यश्नन्ति च दानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Danavas ate the food themselves while children looked on, and likewise ate in front of all the servants."}},{"n":62,"text":"पायसं कृसरं मांसमपूपानथ शष्कुलीः ।\nअपाचयन्नात्मनोऽर्थे वृथामांसान्यभक्षयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They cooked rice-and-milk, kichri, meat, cakes and pastries for themselves, and ate meat needlessly."}},{"n":63,"text":"उत्सूर्यशायिनश्चासन्सर्वे चासन्प्रगेनिशाः ।\nअवर्तन्कलहाश्चात्र दिवारात्रं गृहे गृहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"All slept past sunrise and all slept in the early morning; quarrels went on day and night in house after house."}},{"n":64,"text":"अनार्याश्चार्यमासीनं पर्युपासन्न तत्र ह ।\nआश्रमस्थान्विकर्मस्थाः प्रद्विषन्ति परस्परम् ।\nसंकराश्चाप्यवर्तन्त न च शौचमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ignoble did not wait on the noble who sat there; the householders and those in forbidden work hated each other; mixing arose and purity did not remain."}},{"n":65,"text":"ये च वेदविदो विप्रा विस्पष्टमनृचश्च ये ।\nनिरन्तरविशेषास्ते बहुमानावमानयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmanas who knew the Veda and those who clearly did not were no different from each other in honour or dishonour."}},{"n":66,"text":"हावमाभरणं वेषं गतिं स्थितिमवेक्षितुम् ।\nअसेवन्त भुजिष्या वै दुर्जनाचरितं विधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Servants watched mistresses' gestures, ornaments, dress, gait and stance, and followed the ways of evil people."}},{"n":67,"text":"स्त्रियः पुरुषवेषेण पुंसः स्त्रीवेषधारिणः ।\nक्रीडारतिविहारेषु परां मुदमवाप्नुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women in men's dress and men in women's dress took the greatest joy in games, pleasures and pastimes."}},{"n":68,"text":"प्रभवद्भिः पुरा दायानर्हेभ्यः प्रतिपादितान् ।\nनाभ्यवर्तन्त नास्तिक्याद्वर्तन्तः संभवेष्वपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What had earlier been given by rulers to the unfit, they did not take back, from disbelief, even when occasions arose."}},{"n":69,"text":"मित्रेणाभ्यर्थितं मित्रमर्थे संशयिते क्वचित् ।\nवालकोट्यग्रमात्रेण स्वार्थेनाघ्नत तद्वसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a friend sought help from a friend in need, for a profit of the tip of a hair, they struck down that property."}},{"n":70,"text":"परस्वादानरुचयो विपण्यव्यवहारिणः ।\nअदृश्यन्तार्यवर्णेषु शूद्राश्चापि तपोधनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking others' property pleased them, and they traded in the market; Shudras, rich in austerity, were seen among the noble classes."}},{"n":71,"text":"अधीयन्तेऽव्रताः केचिद्वृथाव्रतमथापरे ।\nअशुश्रूषुर्गुरोः शिष्यः कश्चिच्छिष्यसखो गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some studied without vows, others kept vows in vain; the pupil did not serve the teacher, and the teacher was a pupil's friend."}},{"n":72,"text":"पिता चैव जनित्री च श्रान्तौ वृत्तोत्सवाविव ।\nअप्रभुत्वे स्थितौ वृद्धावन्नं प्रार्थयतः सुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Father and mother, weary, as if their festival was over, helpless and old, begged food from their sons."}},{"n":73,"text":"तत्र वेदविदः प्राज्ञा गाम्भीर्ये सागरोपमाः ।\nकृष्यादिष्वभवन्सक्ता मूर्खाः श्राद्धान्यभुञ्जत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the wise Veda-knowers, deep as the ocean, became attached to farming and the like, and fools ate at funeral feasts."}},{"n":74,"text":"प्रातः प्रातश्च सुप्रश्नं कल्पनं प्रेषणक्रियाः ।\nशिष्यानुप्रहितास्तस्मिन्नकुर्वन्गुरवश्च ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Every morning, the asking of good questions, the arrangement of things and the sending of errands were done by pupils at the teachers' command."}},{"n":75,"text":"श्वश्रूश्वशुरयोरग्रे वधूः प्रेष्यानशासत ।\nअन्वशासच्च भर्तारं समाहूयाभिजल्पती ॥","meaning":{"en":"In front of her mother-in-law and father-in-law the bride ordered the servants, and, calling her husband, spoke and ordered him about."}},{"n":76,"text":"प्रयत्नेनापि चारक्षच्चित्तं पुत्रस्य वै पिता ।\nव्यभजंश्चापि संरम्भाद्दुःखवासं तथावसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A father guarded his son's mind with effort, and they divided up from anger and lived in sorrow."}},{"n":77,"text":"अग्निदाहेन चोरैर्वा राजभिर्वा हृतं धनम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा द्वेषात्प्राहसन्त सुहृत्संभाविता ह्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing wealth taken by fire, thieves or kings, they laughed from malice, even those held dear by friends."}},{"n":78,"text":"कृतघ्ना नास्तिकाः पापा गुरुदाराभिमर्शिनः ।\nअभक्ष्यभक्षणरता निर्मर्यादा हतत्विषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were ungrateful, unbelieving, sinful, violators of the teacher's wife, fond of eating the forbidden, shameless and dull."}},{"n":79,"text":"तेष्वेवमादीनाचारानाचरत्सु विपर्यये ।\nनाहं देवेन्द्र वत्स्यामि दानवेष्विति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they were behaving in these ways and their order was reversed, I decided: Lord of the gods, I will not live among the Danavas."}},{"n":80,"text":"तां मां स्वयमनुप्राप्तामभिनन्द शचीपते ।\nत्वयार्चितां मां देवेश पुरोधास्यन्ति देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Welcome me, Shachi's lord, who have come to you of myself; honoured by you, lord of the gods, I shall be put at the front by the gods."}},{"n":81,"text":"यत्राहं तत्र मत्कान्ता मद्विशिष्टा मदर्पणाः ।\nसप्त देव्यो मयाष्टम्यो वासं चेष्यन्ति मेऽष्टधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where I am, there my dear ones follow, the best and devoted to me: seven goddesses, with me as the eighth, will make their home in eight ways."}},{"n":82,"text":"आशा श्रद्धा धृतिः कान्तिर्विजितिः सन्नतिः क्षमा ।\nअष्टमी वृत्तिरेतासां पुरोगा पाकशासन ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are Asha, Shraddha, Dhriti, Kanti, Vijiti, Sannati, Kshama, and the eighth, Vritti, who leads them, Indra."}},{"n":83,"text":"ताश्चाहं चासुरांस्त्यक्त्वा युष्मद्विषयमागता ।\nत्रिदशेषु निवत्स्यामो धर्मनिष्ठान्तरात्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I and they, having left the asuras, have come to your domain. We shall live among the gods, whose hearts are fixed in dharma."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":84,"text":"इत्युक्तवचनां देवीमत्यर्थं तौ ननन्दतुः ।\nनारदश्च त्रिलोकर्षिर्वृत्रहन्ता च वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard the goddess speak, the two, Narada, sage of the three worlds, and Indra, slayer of Vritra, were exceedingly glad."}},{"n":85,"text":"ततोऽनलसखो वायुः प्रववौ देववेश्मसु ।\nइष्टगन्धः सुखस्पर्शः सर्वेन्द्रियसुखावहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wind, friend of fire, blew through the gods' dwellings, bringing welcome fragrance, pleasant to touch and delighting all the senses."}},{"n":86,"text":"शुचौ चाभ्यर्चिते देशे त्रिदशाः प्रायशः स्थिताः ।\nलक्ष्म्या सहितमासीनं मघवन्तं दिदृक्षवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a pure and honoured place the gods mostly stood, wishing to see Maghavan seated with Lakshmi."}},{"n":87,"text":"ततो दिवं प्राप्य सहस्रलोचनः\nश्रियोपपन्नः सुहृदा सुरर्षिणा ।\nरथेन हर्यश्वयुजा सुरर्षभः\nसदः सुराणामभिसत्कृतो ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the thousand-eyed lord of gods, with Shri and his friend the divine sage, went to heaven in the car yoked with bay horses, and, honoured, entered the assembly of the gods."}},{"n":88,"text":"अथेङ्गितं वज्रधरस्य नारदः\nश्रियाश्च देव्या मनसा विचारयन् ।\nश्रियै शशंसामरदृष्टपौरुषः\nशिवेन तत्रागमनं महर्द्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Narada, pondering in mind the wish of the thunderbolt-bearer and the goddess Shri, whose manliness had been seen by the gods, announced to Shri that they should enter with great and auspicious wealth."}},{"n":89,"text":"ततोऽमृतं द्यौः प्रववर्ष भास्वती\nपितामहस्यायतने स्वयंभुवः ।\nअनाहता दुन्दुभयश्च नेदिरे\nतथा प्रसन्नाश्च दिशश्चकाशिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the shining heaven rained nectar on the dwelling of the Self-born grandfather; unstruck drums sounded, and the quarters shone clear."}},{"n":90,"text":"यथर्तु सस्येषु ववर्ष वासवो\nन धर्ममार्गाद्विचचाल कश्चन ।\nअनेकरत्नाकरभूषणा च भूः\nसुघोषघोषा भुवनौकसां जये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra rained in season on the crops; no one swerved from the path of dharma; the earth, adorned with many jewel-mines, resounded with the glad noise of beings at the victory."}},{"n":91,"text":"क्रियाभिरामा मनुजा यशस्विनो\nबभुः शुभे पुण्यकृतां पथि स्थिताः ।\nनरामराः किंनरयक्षराक्षसाः\nसमृद्धिमन्तः सुखिनो यशस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"People, delighting in their work and renowned, shone, standing on the good path of the virtuous; men, gods, kinnaras, yakshas and rakshasas were prosperous, happy and famed."}},{"n":92,"text":"न जात्वकाले कुसुमं कुतः फलं\nपपात वृक्षात्पवनेरितादपि ।\nरसप्रदाः कामदुघाश्च धेनवो\nन दारुणा वाग्विचचार कस्यचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A flower never fell from a tree out of season, even when blown by wind, let alone fruit; cows gave rich milk and fulfilled wishes; and no one spoke a harsh word."}},{"n":93,"text":"इमां सपर्यां सह सर्वकामदैः\nश्रियाश्च शक्रप्रमुखैश्च दैवतैः ।\nपठन्ति ये विप्रसदः समागमे\nसमृद्धकामाः श्रियमाप्नुवन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who recite this worship of Shri, with the givers of all wishes and the gods led by Indra, in an assembly of the twice-born, have their wishes fulfilled and gain Shri."}},{"n":94,"text":"त्वया कुरूणां वर यत्प्रचोदितं\nभवाभवस्येह परं निदर्शनम् ।\nतदद्य सर्वं परिकीर्तितं मया\nपरीक्ष्य तत्त्वं परिगन्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Kurus, what you asked me, the supreme illustration here of rise and fall, I have now recounted in full; having examined it, you ought to grasp the truth."}}]}]}